def author(c,s,m,a):
 c('b226','節水池耦合、非恆定充洩水與滾動閘門的定量深化~Quantitative extension of basin coupling, unsteady filling and rolling-gate mechanics',['acp-open','acp-basin','acp-dimensions'],r'''
雙池水位均衡~Equalization between two pools||兩個有限面積水體連通時，兩邊水位都會改變，不能把節水池當無限水源。守恆終點只由初始體積與面積決定，達到終點的時間則另受管路控制。~Connecting two finite pools changes both levels, so a saving basin is not an infinite reservoir. Conservation determines the equilibrium endpoint from initial storage and areas, while conduits separately determine how quickly it is approached.||假設閘室面積20000 m²、水位10 m，池面積10000 m²、水位4 m，同基準且斷面固定；均衡水位(20000×10+10000×4)/30000=8 m。~Assume chamber area 20000 m² at level 10 m and basin area 10000 m² at 4 m, common datum and fixed areas. Equalized level is (20000×10+10000×4)/30000=8 m.||各自積分水位變化乘面積，檢查兩側交換體積是否相反相等；再用閥位和流量時序辨識接近均衡時變慢的原因，不能只比較終點。~Integrate area times level change on each side and check equal opposite exchange volumes. Use valve and flow histories to diagnose slowing near equilibrium instead of comparing endpoints alone.||把較小池當固定水頭會高估可回用水量，忽略連通管容積和漏流也會破壞守恆。若兩水位計基準不同，甚至會虛構無法解釋的水量損失。~Treating the smaller basin as fixed head overstates recoverable water. Conduit storage, leakage and mismatched gauge datums can also break the apparent balance and create fictitious unexplained water losses.||節水池面積有限時，其水位不會保持固定。~A finite saving basin does not maintain a fixed water level.
充水歷線與慣性~Filling hydrograph and inertia||船閘水位上升速度取決於當時淨流量，初期加速和末期減速產生的水面坡度又影響船舶受力。平均充水時間無法表示瞬時最大流量。~Lock level rises with instantaneous net flow. Early acceleration and late deceleration also create surface slopes affecting vessels, so average filling time cannot represent peak discharge.||假設三角形充水歷線峰值300 m³/s、總歷時1200 s，水量0.5Qt=180000 m³；閘面積22500 m²則升8 m，非本站運轉歷線。~Assume triangular filling hydrograph with peak 300 m³/s over 1200 s. Volume is 180000 m³ and rise over 22500 m² is 8 m, not a site operating hydrograph.||用流量積分對照水位升幅，並比較室內前後水位差與船舶繫纜負荷；保留流量上升段解析度，避免用整段平均掩蓋慣性效應。~Compare integrated flow with level rise and relate longitudinal level differences to mooring loads. Preserve the rising limb resolution instead of smoothing inertial effects into a full-cycle average.||同一總水量可以由溫和或尖峰歷線達成，船舶受力卻不同。若僅用完成時間驗收，可能漏掉局部流速、壓力振盪和繫纜張力峰值。~Equal total volumes can arise from gentle or peaked hydrographs with different vessel loads. Completion time alone misses local velocities, pressure oscillations and maximum mooring tensions during the filling cycle.||相同充水量與時間不代表相同瞬時水力荷載。~Equal filling volume and duration do not imply equal transient loading.
縱向水面坡度推力~Longitudinal water-slope force||充水不均會使閘室水面形成坡度，船體承受對應的長向壓力差。以排水重量乘小坡度可估算準靜態推力，但需另外處理流速阻力和繫纜動力。~Uneven filling creates a longitudinal surface slope and pressure imbalance on a vessel. Displacement weight times small slope estimates quasi-static force, with current drag and mooring dynamics treated separately.||取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設船舶排水質量50000 t、閘內坡度0.0002，長向力約mgS=98.1 kN；小坡度準靜態，不含阻力與加速度。~Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume vessel displacement mass 50000 t and longitudinal slope 0.0002. Approximate force mgS=98.1 kN, for a small quasi-static slope without drag or acceleration.||在船首船尾及中段量測水位與流速，校核坡度估算和繫纜張力相位；將風力、推進器影響與繫纜剛度分離，建立可重現的比較工況。~Measure levels and currents at bow, stern and midship, comparing inferred slope with mooring-tension phase. Separate wind, propulsion effects and line stiffness to define reproducible comparison conditions.||單一水位站無法辨認室內坡度，繫纜伸長也會造成船體動態放大。若將全部張力歸於水面坡度，可能掩蓋局部射流或不對稱流入。~A single gauge cannot resolve chamber slope, and elastic mooring lines can amplify motion. Attributing all tension to slope may conceal a local jet or asymmetric inflow acting on the hull.||閘室平均水位平穩不代表船首船尾沒有壓力差。~A steady mean level does not exclude bow-to-stern pressure differences.
密度交換前緣~Density-exchange front||海水與淡水連通時，即使兩側表面水位相同，密度差仍可驅動底層鹽水前進和上層淡水返回。這種交換不能用零淨流量判定不存在。~Connected salt and fresh water can exchange through bottom and surface currents even at equal surface elevations. Zero net discharge therefore does not establish absence of density-driven exchange.||取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設密度差25 kg/m³、基準1000 kg/m³、水深5 m，約化重力g′=0.24525 m/s²，速度尺度√(g′h)=1.107 m/s；非精確前緣速度。~Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume density difference 25 kg/m³, reference density 1000 kg/m³ and depth 5 m. Reduced gravity is 0.24525 m/s² and √(g′h)=1.107 m/s, a scale rather than an exact front speed.||同時量測上下層流向及鹽度，計算鹽通量而非只積分總流量；追蹤前緣與船舶排水的交互作用，避免把短時混濁當作鹽分證據。~Measure upper and lower currents and salinity together, calculating salt flux rather than total discharge alone. Track interactions with vessel displacement and avoid treating turbidity as direct evidence of salinity.||表層看似沒有入流時底層仍可向內輸送鹽分，傳感器只設單一深度會漏判。強紊流又會改變界面厚度，使理想兩層模型失效。~Salt can enter along the bed while the surface appears still, making one-depth sensing inadequate. Strong turbulence thickens the interface and can invalidate an ideal two-layer description of exchange.||兩側水面相同不代表兩種密度水體停止交換。~Equal surface levels do not stop exchange between different-density waters.
閘門浮力與輪載~Gate buoyancy and wheel loads||滾動門靠輪組與浮力共同承受重量，水位改變會重新分配輪載。減輕平均輪載有利移動，但偏心、軌道沉降和門體變形仍可能使個別輪子受力集中。~Rolling gates share weight between buoyancy and wheel groups, with levels changing wheel loads. Lower mean loading aids movement, but eccentricity, rail settlement and deformation can still concentrate reactions on individual wheels.||假設門重40 MN、浮力28 MN、8輪理想均分，平均輪載(40−28)/8=1.5 MN；不含偏心、動力或軌道高差。~Assume gate weight 40 MN, buoyancy 28 MN and eight equally sharing wheels. Mean wheel load is (40−28)/8=1.5 MN, excluding eccentricity, dynamics and rail-level differences.||將輪載或軸承應變與水位、門位一起比對，檢查軌道高程和各輪接觸；以總反力守恆確認量測，再評估最大輪載而非平均值。~Compare wheel loads or bearing strains with water level and position, checking rail elevation and wheel contact. Verify total reaction equilibrium before evaluating maximum individual loads rather than averages.||某輪懸空會把荷載轉給其他輪，平均公式仍可能看似正常。浮力艙漏水也可能增加荷載而不立即停止運動，所以移動成功不能代替承載檢查。~A lifted wheel transfers load to others while the average formula still appears normal. A leaking buoyancy compartment can increase loading without stopping motion, so movement success cannot replace bearing assessment.||平均輪載低不代表每一個輪組都沒有超載。~Low average wheel load does not exclude an overloaded individual wheel.
管路快速減速壓峰~Rapid conduit deceleration pressure||充洩水管路的速度改變會形成壓力波，反射邊界和含氣量決定波速與衰減。Joukowsky式適合快速改變的初估，慢速閥動作須用歷時模型。~Velocity changes in filling conduits create pressure waves whose speed and decay depend on boundaries and air content. Joukowsky gives a rapid-change estimate; slower valve motion requires time-dependent analysis.||假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、波速800 m/s、速度減少0.3 m/s且變化快於2L/a，Δp=ρaΔv=240 kPa；非閥門操作設定。~Assume density 1000 kg/m³, wave speed 800 m/s and velocity change 0.3 m/s occurring faster than 2L/a. Δp=ρaΔv=240 kPa, not a valve operating setting.||核對管長、波速和動作歷時，再比較多點壓力到達時間與反射；檢查記錄取樣率足以看到波峰，並辨識氣穴與單相彈性模型的差別。~Check pipe length, wave speed and movement duration, comparing pressure arrival and reflection at several locations. Verify adequate sampling and distinguish vapor cavities from the single-phase elastic model.||若壓力降至汽化壓以下，水柱分離後再碰撞可能產生不同峰值，單次線性式失效。把壓力計阻尼造成的平滑當成真實衰減也會低估荷載。~Column separation below vapor pressure and subsequent recombination can create different peaks, invalidating a single linear estimate. Sensor damping mistaken for physical decay can also underestimate the actual transient load.||慢速水流變化不能直接套用快速水錘的完整壓峰。~Slow velocity changes cannot automatically receive the full rapid-waterhammer peak.
混凝土溫差拘束~Concrete thermal restraint||大型閘室牆體的溫度收縮受底板與相鄰澆塊拘束，裂縫風險取決於拘束和早齡強度發展。只看最高溫度會漏掉冷卻過程的拉應力。~Large lock walls contract against foundations and adjoining blocks. Crack risk depends on restraint and developing early-age strength, so peak temperature alone misses tensile demand during cooling.||假設E=25 GPa、熱膨脹係數10⁻⁵/K、降溫15 K、有效拘束0.4，σ=REαΔT=1.5 MPa；彈性近似，未含徐變鬆弛。~Assume E=25 GPa, thermal expansion 10⁻⁵/K, cooling 15 K and effective restraint 0.4. Stress REαΔT=1.5 MPa, an elastic estimate without creep relaxation.||將核心與表面溫度、接縫位移和齡期強度同步比較，辨認內外溫差與整體拘束；使用實際材料試驗修正模數，保留養護期間邊界。~Compare core and surface temperatures, joint movement and age-dependent strength synchronously. Distinguish internal gradients from overall restraint and use material tests to update modulus and curing boundaries.||表面快速冷卻會造成局部裂縫，即使整體平均溫降不大；徐變雖降低短時應力，也不能保證止水接縫保持完整。以成熟度單值代替拉伸能力容易誤判。~Rapid surface cooling can crack concrete despite a small mean drop. Creep reduces some stresses but does not guarantee watertight joints, and one maturity value cannot substitute for tensile capacity.||最高溫度相同的澆塊仍可能有不同熱裂縫風險。~Blocks with the same peak temperature can have different thermal-cracking risks.
船底餘裕與沉降量~Under-keel clearance and squat||船底淨空由水深減吃水和動態變化決定，載重、鹽度和航速都會影響結果。幾何餘裕不是可直接使用的航行餘裕，須分列波動與量測不確定度。~Under-keel clearance subtracts draft and dynamic effects from depth, with loading, salinity and speed all relevant. Geometric clearance differs from usable navigation margin, requiring separate motion and measurement allowances.||假設水深16 m、吃水14.5 m、動態下沉0.25 m、其他保留0.35 m，可用餘裕16−14.5−0.25−0.35=0.90 m；全部為假設。~Assume depth 16 m, draft 14.5 m, squat 0.25 m and other allowance 0.35 m. Available margin is 16−14.5−0.25−0.35=0.90 m, with all values assumed.||統一水深、吃水和潮位的基準與時刻，查底床最高點而非平均深度；將船體縱傾、波動和測深誤差分別保存，避免重複或遺漏扣減。~Align depth, draft and tide references and times, checking highest bed points rather than mean depth. Retain trim, motion and sounding uncertainty separately to avoid duplicated or omitted deductions.||沉積高點可能在水深平均值仍足夠時造成局部淺區，密度改變亦會增加吃水。若把固定吃水值用於所有載重與水質，會產生不實的可用餘裕。~A deposit high spot can create a shallow patch despite adequate mean depth, and density changes alter draft. Fixed draft across different loads and water conditions creates a misleading available margin.||測得平均水深足夠不代表整條船底通道均足夠深。~Adequate mean depth does not establish clearance along the full hull route.
回用率與淨淡水耗用~Reuse ratio and net freshwater use||回用百分比必須有明確分母，閘室交換量、從湖取水量與全年水源消耗並不相同。漏流、蒸發與鹽分管理可能改變系統邊界內的淨耗用。~A reuse percentage requires an explicit denominator. Chamber exchange, lake withdrawal and annual water-resource consumption differ, while leakage, evaporation and salinity management can change net use within the chosen boundary.||假設一次交換量200000 m³、回用率0.6、另有損失5000 m³，淡水補充=(1−0.6)200000+5000=85000 m³；非官方每次用水量。~Assume cycle exchange 200000 m³, reuse fraction 0.6 and other losses 5000 m³. Freshwater makeup is (1−0.6)200000+5000=85000 m³, not an official lockage demand.||為每個水量畫清楚來源與去向，將暫存池、外海與淡水湖分成控制體；確認計量時間覆蓋完整循環，並說明船舶排水體積是否納入。~Map every water source and destination, separating basins, sea and freshwater lake into control volumes. Cover a complete cycle and state whether vessel displacement is included in the metering boundary.||只引用回用率而省略其他損失，會把單次水力效率誤當流域節水。閘次船型差異和不完整循環又可能造成看似改善卻不可比較的績效數字。~Quoting reuse alone confuses cycle hydraulics with watershed savings. Vessel differences and incomplete cycles can produce apparently improved performance values that are not comparable across the measurement period.||百分之六十回用不等於全年淡水需求直接減少六成。~Sixty percent reuse does not directly imply sixty percent lower annual freshwater demand.
故障停航與水源緩衝~Outage backlog and water reserve||容量與水源限制可能交互作用，故障後即使機械恢復，也需要足夠淡水與航道時間清理隊列。系統復原應同時盤點通行和水量資源。~Capacity and water availability interact: after mechanical restoration, clearing a backlog also needs freshwater and navigation time. Recovery therefore requires both transit and water-resource accounting.||假設積壓8次通行、每次教學補水85000 m³，額外需求680000 m³；若可分配水量每日170000 m³，至少需4 days，不含新增需求。~Assume eight queued transits each needing teaching makeup 85000 m³. Extra demand is 680000 m³; allocation 170000 m³/day requires at least four days, excluding new arrivals.||用匿名化通行隊列、可分配水量與其他取水用途建立共同日曆；將已確認的供水約束和可調整排程分開，核對每項需求是否重複計列。~Build a common calendar of anonymous transit queues, available water and other withdrawals. Separate confirmed supply constraints from adjustable schedules and check that demands are not counted twice.||機械最大吞吐量可能遠高於水源允許速率，忽略這點會提出無法實現的復原計畫。若水位下降又增加抽水或通航限制，簡單固定單次需求亦會改變。~Mechanical throughput can exceed water-limited capacity, making a recovery plan infeasible. Falling levels can introduce further pumping or navigation constraints and change the assumed fixed water demand per transit.||設備復原並不表示積壓通行能按機械最快速度完成。~Equipment recovery does not guarantee clearing the queue at maximum mechanical throughput.
''')
 for i,ex,out,un in [(1,'(20000*10+10000*4)/30000',8,'m'),(2,'.5*300*1200/22500',8,'m'),(3,'50000*1000*9.81*.0002/1000',98.1,'kN'),(4,'math.sqrt(9.81*25/1000*5)',1.1073617,'m/s'),(5,'(40-28)/8',1.5,'MN'),(6,'1000*800*.3/1000',240,'kPa'),(7,'.4*25e9*1e-5*15/1e6',1.5,'MPa'),(8,'16-14.5-.25-.35',.9,'m'),(9,'(1-.6)*200000+5000',85000,'m3'),(10,'8*85000/170000',4,'days')]:a('b226',i,ex,out,un)
 c('b227','高提升船廂的配重、齒條同步與對接邊界~Counterweights, rack synchronization and docking boundaries of a high-lift caisson',['ctg-trial','ctg-function','ctg-history'],r'''
船舶排水與船廂質量~Vessel displacement and caisson mass||浮船進入保持固定水位的船廂時，會排出等重的水，因此船加水總重近似不變。這個平衡依賴船舶自由浮動及水量能夠交換，不能套用坐底或封閉增水情況。~A floating vessel entering a fixed-level caisson displaces water of equal weight, keeping vessel-plus-water mass approximately constant. This requires free flotation and water exchange, and does not apply to grounding or added water in a sealed chamber.||假設船舶質量2000 t、淡水密度1000 kg/m³，排水2000 m³；若維持水位，移出水質量2000 t，理想船廂總質量變化0 t。~Assume vessel mass 2000 t and freshwater density 1000 kg/m³. It displaces 2000 m³; maintaining level removes 2000 t of water, giving ideal total mass change zero tonnes.||用進出船前後水位、船舶排水資料與交換水量交叉核對，不使用載重噸代替排水量；另記錄繫纜是否向船廂施加豎向分力。~Cross-check pre-entry and post-entry levels, vessel displacement and exchanged water. Do not substitute deadweight for displacement, and record whether moorings apply vertical forces to the caisson.||船舶坐底後不再完整由浮力支承，水位改變也會破壞固定總重假設。若混淆載貨重量和船舶總排水質量，平衡重判讀將出現大幅偏差。~Grounding removes full buoyant support, while changing level breaks constant total mass. Confusing cargo weight with total vessel displacement can cause a large error in interpreting counterweight balance.||船越重不必然讓保持水位的浮船船廂總重增加。~A heavier floating vessel need not increase a constant-level caisson total mass.
配重不平衡功率~Counterweight imbalance power||配重抵銷大部分重力，但驅動仍需克服不平衡、摩擦與加速度。把整個提升重量乘高度當成電力耗用，會忽略下降配重釋放的位能。~Counterweights offset most gravity, but drives still overcome imbalance, friction and acceleration. Multiplying total lifted weight by height overstates electrical demand by ignoring potential energy released by descending counterweights.||取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設不平衡質量100 t、速度0.2 m/s，純重力功率Δmgv=196.2 kW；另有摩擦與效率損失，非整機額定功率。~Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume imbalance mass 100 t and speed 0.2 m/s. Gravity-only power Δmgv=196.2 kW, before friction and efficiency losses and distinct from machine-rated power.||同步比較電功率、速度和船廂水位，區分恆速段與加減速段；在相反方向相同條件下比較損失，避免將回生電力誤記為負摩擦。~Compare power, speed and water level synchronously, separating steady motion from acceleration. Compare opposite directions under matched conditions and avoid interpreting regenerated electricity as negative friction.||配重失配可能由漏水或水位偏差引起，單靠驅動電流無法辨認來源。若效率和摩擦隨溫度變動仍視為固定，剩餘荷載的推估便會偏移。~Counterweight mismatch may arise from leakage or level error, which current alone cannot distinguish. Temperature-dependent efficiency and friction shift the inferred residual load if incorrectly treated as constant.||有配重不代表驅動不需要克服任何重力差。~Counterweights do not eliminate every gravitational imbalance in the drive.
齒條切向力分配~Rack tangential-force sharing||齒輪齒條把轉矩轉成豎向力，多驅動點必須協調分擔。平均轉矩相同不保證齒面接觸相同，幾何誤差和傳動剛度會造成局部偏載。~Rack-and-pinion drives convert torque to vertical force and must coordinate several lifting points. Equal mean torque does not ensure equal tooth contact because geometric error and drivetrain stiffness create local unequal loading.||假設單齒輪轉矩200 kN·m、節圓半徑0.5 m，切向力T/r=400 kN；只算理想接觸合力，不含齒形應力集中。~Assume pinion torque 200 kN·m and pitch radius 0.5 m. Tangential force T/r=400 kN, an ideal contact resultant excluding tooth-root stress concentration.||對照軸扭矩、齒條位移及接觸印痕，核查各驅動點的相位與幾何校準；把單齒接觸和多齒分擔的假設寫入局部強度模型。~Compare shaft torque, rack displacement and contact patterns, checking phase and geometric calibration at each drive. State single-tooth versus multiple-tooth sharing assumptions in the local strength model.||一個驅動點遲滯會使其他點先承載，扭矩平均值可能仍正常。齒根疲勞、潤滑不足與齒面點蝕是不同機制，不能僅由總提升力判定。~A lagging drive shifts load to other points despite an apparently normal mean torque. Root fatigue, poor lubrication and contact pitting differ, and total lifting force cannot distinguish these mechanisms.||平均驅動轉矩相同不代表每個齒面受力相同。~Equal average drive torques do not imply equal tooth contact loads.
四角同步與船廂傾斜~Corner synchronization and caisson tilt||大型船廂由多點支承，位置差會轉成傾斜與扭曲，進而改變導向和對接條件。同步控制須比較同基準位置，不能只比較各馬達轉速。~A caisson supported at several points converts position differences into tilt and distortion, affecting guidance and docking. Synchronization requires common-reference positions rather than motor speeds alone.||假設橫向支承跨20 m、兩側高差4 mm，小角度θ=0.004/20=0.0002 rad，即0.01146°；剛體近似不含扭曲。~Assume transverse support spacing 20 m and level difference 4 mm. Small-angle θ=0.004/20=0.0002 rad, or 0.01146 degrees, for rigid motion without distortion.||用獨立測量基準核對多點編碼器與傾角計，分離剛體傾斜和船廂撓曲；記錄同步誤差隨高度與方向的變化，找出重複性模式。~Check encoders and inclinometers against independent survey references, separating rigid tilt from caisson bending. Track synchronization error against elevation and direction to identify repeatable patterns.||兩側編碼器共同零點漂移會讓同步數字好看卻整體偏離對接高程。只比較速度不能發現先前累積的位置差，也不能排除導向件局部卡阻。~Common encoder drift can hide an incorrect docking elevation despite good relative synchronization. Speed comparison misses accumulated position error and does not exclude localized binding in guidance components.||轉速一致不能證明所有支承點的位置已同步。~Equal speeds do not prove synchronized support-point positions.
鋼索彈伸與溫度~Rope extension and temperature||鋼索受力會伸長，等長索因有效剛度和溫度差也可能產生不同位移。鋼索等效模數與實心鋼棒不同，必須使用實測或供應者資料。~Loaded ropes extend, and equal initial lengths can move differently because of stiffness and temperature. Rope effective modulus differs from a solid steel bar and requires measured or supplier-supported values.||假設單索力1 MN、長100 m、有效面積0.005 m²、等效E=100 GPa，ΔL=FL/EA=0.20 m；忽略構造伸長與蠕變。~Assume rope force 1 MN, length 100 m, effective area 0.005 m² and equivalent E=100 GPa. ΔL=FL/EA=0.20 m, excluding constructional stretch and creep.||同時記錄索力、長度基準與溫度，分離載重彈伸和永久伸長；核對繩股結構、端接滑移及模數定義，避免誤用鋼材名義彈性模數。~Record tension, reference length and temperature together, separating elastic from permanent extension. Check strand construction, anchorage slip and modulus definition instead of using nominal solid-steel elasticity.||端接滑移可能表現為長度增加卻不符合索力變化，斷絲也會降低有效剛度。若把所有延伸都視為可逆彈性，便會漏掉需獨立檢查的損傷。~Anchorage slip produces extension inconsistent with tension, and broken wires reduce effective stiffness. Treating all elongation as reversible elasticity misses damage that requires an independent physical inspection.||鋼索的等效彈性模數不可直接當作實心鋼棒模數。~A rope effective modulus is not automatically a solid-bar modulus.
螺旋機構自鎖判讀~Self-locking of screw mechanisms||螺旋升降或安全機構的自鎖與導程角、摩擦和牙型有關。靜態幾何比較可解釋反驅趨勢，不能替代實際安全裝置的設計和動態試驗。~Screw self-locking depends on lead angle, friction and thread form. A static geometric comparison explains back-driving tendency without replacing the design and dynamic verification of a real safety mechanism.||假設理想方牙螺旋導程角3°、摩擦係數0.08，tan3°=0.0524小於0.08，靜態模型有自鎖趨勢；未含振動、潤滑變動與其他牙型。~Assume an ideal square thread with lead angle three degrees and friction coefficient 0.08. tan3°=0.0524 below 0.08 suggests static self-locking, excluding vibration, lubrication change and other thread forms.||核對實際牙型、摩擦試驗和潤滑狀況，將靜態判讀與獨立制動功能分開；在工程文件中追蹤哪些結論來自理論，哪些已有設備驗證。~Check actual thread form, friction testing and lubrication, separating static interpretation from independent braking functions. Track which conclusions are theoretical and which have equipment-specific verification.||潤滑使摩擦降低可能改變反驅條件，動態衝擊也不服從單純靜摩擦比較。若把自鎖當成不需檢查的永久特性，會忽略磨耗和污染造成的改變。~Lubrication can lower friction enough to change back-driving behavior, and impacts do not follow a simple static comparison. Treating self-locking as permanent ignores wear and contamination that alter the mechanism.||螺旋機構靜態自鎖不等於所有動態情況都安全。~Static screw self-locking does not establish safety under every dynamic condition.
對接水位差作用~Docking head-difference force||船廂與航道對接前後，微小水位差也可能在大面積上形成顯著合力。對接荷載需區分平衡水位、間隙充水和結構鎖定，不可只憑水面看似齊平。~Small level differences across a large docking area can create substantial forces. Docking assessment separates equalized levels, gap filling and structural restraint instead of relying on water surfaces that merely appear aligned.||取淡水密度ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²。假設兩側平均壓差來自0.10 m淡水頭、有效面積100 m²，F=ρgΔhA=98.1 kN；均勻壓差只適用共同浸沒區近似。~Use freshwater density ρ=1000 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s². Assume mean pressure difference from 0.10 m freshwater head over 100 m². F=ρgΔhA=98.1 kN, using a uniform difference over a commonly submerged area.||以同基準水位計和對接位移量測核對壓差，將間隙水量與密封受力一起記錄；檢查波浪和船舶移動是否使平均值掩蓋瞬時峰值。~Check head with common-datum gauges and docking displacement, recording gap volume and seal forces together. Examine whether waves and vessel movement hide transient peaks behind an average value.||波動水面可能在平均齊平時仍產生交變荷載，鎖定件間隙又會造成撞擊。若只測一側水位，無法區分船廂升沉和航道自身水位變動。~Fluctuating surfaces create alternating loads even when means match, while locking clearance can cause impact. One-sided level sensing cannot separate caisson movement from changes in the navigation reach itself.||肉眼看似齊平的水面仍可能形成可觀對接荷載。~Visually aligned water surfaces can still generate substantial docking loads.
啟停加速度與慣性~Start-stop acceleration and inertia||即使重量被配重抵銷，船廂和配重的慣性仍需要驅動與制動。加速時兩者動能同時增加，不能將淨重量小誤當總慣性小。~Counterbalancing weight does not remove caisson and counterweight inertia. Both gain kinetic energy during acceleration, so small net weight does not imply small total inertial demand.||假設兩側總移動質量30 million kg、加速度0.005 m/s²，慣性力ma=150 kN；簡化等效平動質量，未含旋轉件慣量。~Assume total moving mass 30 million kg and acceleration 0.005 m/s². Inertial force ma=150 kN, using equivalent translation and excluding rotating-component inertia.||從位置資料以適當濾波求速度和加速度，保留濾波延遲說明；比較驅動力變化與理論慣性項，並把摩擦和不平衡重力另外估計。~Derive speed and acceleration from position using documented filtering and delay. Compare drive-force changes with predicted inertia, estimating friction and gravitational imbalance as separate terms.||直接二次微分雜訊會產生假的加速度峰值，過度平滑又會漏掉衝擊。若不計配重慣性，模型會把正常加速需求誤認為摩擦突然變大。~Differentiating noise twice creates false acceleration peaks, while excessive smoothing hides impacts. Omitting counterweight inertia can make ordinary acceleration demand appear to be a sudden increase in friction.||配重平衡重力後，整個運動系統的慣性仍存在。~Gravity balance leaves the inertia of the moving system intact.
塔柱溫度與對中~Tower temperature and alignment||高塔受日照與季節溫度變化會伸縮，導軌相對位置因此改變。均勻伸長和橫向溫差彎曲是不同機制，應用獨立幾何量測辨認。~Tall towers expand with solar and seasonal temperature changes, shifting guide alignment. Uniform extension differs from curvature caused by transverse thermal gradients and requires independent geometric observations.||假設有效塔高120 m、混凝土熱膨脹係數10⁻⁵/K、均勻升溫10 K，伸長αLΔT=12 mm；不含溫差彎曲與徐變。~Assume effective tower height 120 m, concrete thermal expansion 10⁻⁵/K and uniform warming 10 K. Extension αLΔT=12 mm, excluding thermal curvature and creep.||把塔柱不同方位溫度、測量基準和導軌位置同步，分離日循環與長期沉降；在相似溫度條件下比較年度幾何，而非直接比較任意兩天。~Synchronize temperatures on different faces, survey references and rail positions. Separate daily cycles from long-term settlement and compare annual geometry at similar thermal conditions rather than arbitrary dates.||日照不均造成的彎曲可能比平均溫升更影響導向，測站自身也會熱變形。若把可逆日變化當永久沉降，可能誤導對中診斷和維護優先次序。~Uneven solar heating can affect guidance more than mean warming, and survey stations can also deform thermally. Mistaking reversible daily movement for settlement misdirects alignment diagnosis and maintenance priorities.||塔柱溫度變化不能只用單一平均溫度描述。~One mean temperature cannot describe every thermally induced tower movement.
全流程時間與容量~Full-cycle time and capacity||提升速度只決定垂直運動的一段時間，通航能力還包含進出船、對接與確認。以單程升降時間推算每日通過量，會高估系統容量。~Lift speed controls only the vertical-motion portion of a transit. Entry, exit, docking and confirmation also consume time, so movement time alone overstates daily system capacity.||假設提升100 m、速度0.2 m/s，恆速需500 s；另有進出與對接1300 s，循環1800 s，理想每小時2 cycles，不含停機。~Assume lift 100 m at 0.2 m/s, requiring 500 s at constant speed. Adding 1300 s for entry, exit and docking gives 1800 s and ideal two cycles per hour, excluding outages.||按功能拆分時間戳並保留船型與方向，核對哪些活動能重疊、哪些必須先後完成；把理論上限、實際服務率和維護不可用時間分開呈現。~Split timestamps by function and retain vessel type and direction. Identify overlapping versus sequential activities, separating theoretical upper capacity, observed service rate and maintenance unavailability.||假設所有活動都能重疊會把必要的對接與確認時間刪掉，長船與不同水位也可能改變耗時。以最短一次通過代表全年績效，會隱藏排隊和可用度差異。~Assuming universal overlap removes necessary docking and confirmation time, while vessel length and levels change durations. Using the fastest transit as annual performance hides queues and availability differences.||提升速度最快並不一定帶來最大的全年通航量。~The fastest lift speed does not necessarily maximize annual throughput.
''')
 for i,ex,out,un in [(1,'2000*1000/1000',2000,'m3'),(2,'100*1000*9.81*.2/1000',196.2,'kW'),(3,'200/.5',400,'kN'),(4,'.004/20*180/math.pi',.01145916,'degree'),(5,'1e6*100/(100e9*.005)',.2,'m'),(6,'math.tan(3*math.pi/180)',.05240778,'ratio'),(7,'1000*9.81*.1*100/1000',98.1,'kN'),(8,'30e6*.005/1000',150,'kN'),(9,'1e-5*120*10*1000',12,'mm'),(10,'3600/(100/.2+1300)',2,'cycles/h')]:a('b227',i,ex,out,un)
